roject material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Citation and original explanation; linked external bodies are not included.\",\"subject_id\":\"claim:heterogeneity-outcome-scales\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Outcome encoding, link, target covariate distribution and exposure are declared.\",\"Main effects and treatment interactions use a full-rank design.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:f8049ffccf7f14ae9befe7e3\",\"object_id\":\"heterogeneity.categorical\",\"predicate\":\"qualifies\",\"provenance\":[\"source:note:heterogeneity-outcome-scales\",\"source:ontology:knol2012\",\"source:ontology:statsmodels-glm\",\"hernan2020\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original methodological explanation checked against linked primary sources; no independent human review or study audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-14\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_context_review\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Scoped methodological explanation; not a study finding or a promise of identification.\",\"subject_id\":\"claim:heterogeneity-outcome-scales\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original methodological explanation checked against linked primary sources; no independent human review or study audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-14\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_context_review\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Scoped methodological explanation; not a study finding or a promise of identification.\",\"source_ids\":[\"source:note:heterogeneity-outcome-scales\",\"source:ontology:knol2012\",\"source:ontology:statsmodels-glm\",\"hernan2020\"],\"summary\":\"An identity-link interaction concerns a conditional mean difference, a logit interaction concerns conditional log odds ratios, and a log-link interaction concerns conditional mean ratios. Standardized risk or mean differences are different functionals and require contrasts of their own predictions and covariance. A count-rate model additionally defines exposure and an offset; compare predictions at a stated exposure. Robust standard errors cannot repair a wrong mean model, inadequate overlap or unmeasured confounding.\",\"title\":\"Outcome families require distinct interaction targets\"}" .
