edistributed.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_context_review\",\"sources\":[\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Scoped original methodological explanation; no whole-method or study audit is implied.\",\"subject_id\":\"claim:longitudinal-feedback\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"The intended longitudinal strategy and sequential identification conditions are stated.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:ff67320bc679f93e636c807c\",\"object_id\":\"long.g_estimation\",\"predicate\":\"qualifies\",\"provenance\":[\"source:note:longitudinal-feedback\",\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original note reviewed against linked primary context; no external full text redistributed.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_context_review\",\"sources\":[\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Scoped original methodological explanation; no whole-method or study audit is implied.\",\"subject_id\":\"claim:longitudinal-feedback\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original note reviewed against linked primary context; no external full text redistributed.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_context_review\",\"sources\":[\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Scoped original methodological explanation; no whole-method or study audit is implied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"source:note:longitudinal-feedback\",\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"summary\":\"When a measured covariate is affected by earlier treatment and predicts later treatment and outcome, ordinary covariate adjustment can fail to target the intended treatment-history effect. Define the intervention history and order its measurements. Marginal structural models, longitudinal g-computation and structural-model approaches use different estimation constructions, but all require their applicable sequential exchangeability, consistency and support conditions; fitted histories do not verify those assumptions.\",\"title\":\"Treatment-confounder feedback requires sequential reasoning\"}" .
