effect as a function of how reluctant a unit is to be treated, instead of reporting one local average.\",\"title\":\"Marginal treatment effects\"}" .
<urn:capy:iv.shift_share> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Shift-share (Bartik) instruments" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:iv.shift_share\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:iv.shift_share\",\"citation_ids\":[\"source:unresolved:1ee18c5fc5f44546d70f\",\"source:unresolved:c6db1e60c6205a0b10d2\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":\"Not wrapped. Two-stage least squares with your own constructed instrument is implemented.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":false,\"r\":\"ShiftShareSE\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"ShiftShareSE\"],\"runs_here\":false,\"summary\":\"Not built into the app yet. The authoritative version is the R package ShiftShareSE, which the Engines screen can install for you.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.iv\",\"id\":\"iv\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"An instrument or encouragement changed treatment, not the outcome directly.\",\"title\":\"Something else pushed people in\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.first_stage\",\"id\":\"first_stage\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"First stage\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.reduced_form\",\"id\":\"reduced_form\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Reduced form\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.overid\",\"id\":\"overid\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Overidentification test\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"LATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.late\",\"id\":\"LATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who only got it because of the instrument or the cutoff, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Local average treatment effect\"},{\"acronym\":\"ATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.ate\",\"id\":\"ATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"If everyone got the programme, how would the average outcome change?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.shift_share\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"iv.shift_share\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Combine national shocks with local exposure shares to build an instrument for local changes.\",\"options\":[],\"plain_language\":\"Combine national shocks with local exposure shares to build an instrument for local changes.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"}],\"references\":[\"Goldsmith-Pinkham, Sorkin & Swift (2020)\",\"Borusyak, Hull & Jaravel (2022)\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[],\"roles_optional\":[],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\",\"an instrument\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.iv\",\"id\":\"iv\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"An instrument or encouragement changed treatment, not the outcome directly.\",\"title\":\"Something else pushed people in\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.bounds.manski\",\"id\":\"bounds.manski\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Report the range the effect must lie in given only what the data can support, without assuming away the missing counterfactual.\",\"title\":\"Manski bounds\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.2sls\",\"id\":\"iv.2sls\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Use only the part of the treatment that the instrument moved, and see what happened to the outcome.\",\"title\":\"Two-stage least squares\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.gmm\",\"id\":\"iv.gmm\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Weight the instruments by how informative each one actually is, using a weight matrix estimated from the data.\",\"title\":\"Two-step GMM\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.liml\",\"id\":\"iv.liml\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"The maximum-likelihood cousin of two-stage least squares, which stays much better behaved when the instruments are weak.\",\"title\":\"LIML (and Fuller)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.mte\",\"id\":\"iv.mte\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Trace the effect as a function of how reluctant a unit is to be treated, instead of reporting one local average.\",\"title\":\"Marginal treatment effects\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.weak_robust\",\"id\":\"iv.weak_robust\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Report the set of effects the data cannot reject, which stays honest however weak the instrument is.\",\"title\":\"Weak-instrument-robust confidence set\"}],\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"status_label\":\"Reasonable\",\"tags\":[\"Something else pushed people in\",\"LATE\",\"ATE\",\"Reasonable\"],\"title\":\"Shift-share (Bartik) instruments\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.relevance\",\"explains\":\"The instrument actually moves treatment, and moves it enough that the resulting estimate is not mostly noise.\",\"id\":\"relevance\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Instrument relevance\",\"worry_when\":\"An effective F below about 10; a first-stage coefficient that is substantively tiny even if statistically significant; many instruments.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exclusion\",\"explains\":\"The instrument affects the outcome only through the treatment. On the board, that is the arrow you did not draw.\",\"id\":\"exclusion\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exclusion restriction\",\"worry_when\":\"The instrument is a policy that changed several things at once; it is correlated with geography, time or institutions that have their own effects; it was chosen because it predicted the outcome.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.monotonicity\",\"explains\":\"The instrument pushes everyone the same way, or not at all. Nobody takes the treatment only because they were discouraged from it.\",\"id\":\"monotonicity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Monotonicity / no defiers\",\"worry_when\":\"The instrument is an incentive that could plausibly backfire for some people, or it is a judge or examiner whose leniency ordering differs across case types.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"The identifying assumption sits either on the shares or on the shocks, and which one you are claiming changes both the standard errors and the plausibility. Standard errors that ignore the shared shock structure are far too small.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"The workhorse instrument in regional and trade economics, and there is now a settled account of what exactly has to be exogenous.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"iv.shift_share\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"iv.shift_share\",\"registry\":{\"coming\":\"Not wrapped. Two-stage least squares with your own constructed instrument is implemented.\",\"designs\":[\"iv\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"first_stage\",\"reduced_form\",\"overid\"],\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":false,\"r\":\"ShiftShareSE\"},\"estimands\":[\"LATE\",\"ATE\"],\"id\":\"iv.shift_share\",\"one_liner\":\"Combine national shocks with local exposure shares to build an instrument for local changes.\",\"probes\":[\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"probe.alternate_spec\"],\"r_needs\":[\"ShiftShareSE\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:1ee18c5fc5f44546d70f\",\"requested_as\":\"Goldsmith-Pinkham, Sorkin & Swift (2020)\"},{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:c6db1e60c6205a0b10d2\",\"requested_as\":\"Borusyak, Hull & Jaravel (2022)\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"source:unresolved:1ee18c5fc5f44546d70f\",\"source:unresolved:c6db1e60c6205a0b10d2\"],\"references\":[\"Goldsmith-Pinkham, Sorkin & Swift (2020)\",\"Borusyak, Hull & Jaravel (2022)\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"outcome\",\"instruments\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/registry/methods.extra.yaml\",\"source_sha256\":\"2cb349e9f7f7e6f88c10c18d81478656fd420eda7ca977d9767610ac8c7a4be0\",\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"title\":\"Shift-share (Bartik) instruments\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"The identifying assumption sits either on the shares or on the shocks, and which one you are claiming changes both the standard errors and the plausibility. Standard errors that ignore the shared shock structure are far too small.\",\"why_recommended\":\"The workhorse instrument in regional and trade economics, and there is now a settled account of what exactly has to be exogenous.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:039cd5e937802dda1361e942\",\"object_id\":\"concept:mte\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"angrist1996\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"iv.shift_share\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:0b961a3d57558da19f8ae823\",\"object_id\":\"estimand:LATE\",\"predicate\":\"targets_estimand\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"act