ginal or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"iv.shift_share\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Combine national shocks with local exposure shares to build an instrument for local changes.\",\"title\":\"Shift-share (Bartik) instruments\"}" .
<urn:capy:iv.weak_robust> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Weak-instrument-robust confidence set" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:iv.weak_robust\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:iv.weak_robust\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1111/1468-0262.00438\",\"10.1214/aoms/1177730090\",\"10.1257/aer.20211063\",\"source:unresolved:4eccf47fd5ff40c6c9f1\",\"source:unresolved:df637410f69a1d8930a5\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"ivmodel\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"ivmodel\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.iv\",\"id\":\"iv\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"An instrument or encouragement changed treatment, not the outcome directly.\",\"title\":\"Something else pushed people in\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.first_stage\",\"id\":\"first_stage\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"First stage\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.reduced_form\",\"id\":\"reduced_form\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Reduced form\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.overid\",\"id\":\"overid\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Overidentification test\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.weak_iv_set\",\"id\":\"weak_iv_set\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Weak-instrument-robust set\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.endogeneity\",\"id\":\"endogeneity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Endogeneity test\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.compliers\",\"id\":\"compliers\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Complier share\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.placebo_reduced_form\",\"id\":\"placebo_reduced_form\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Placebo reduced form\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"LATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.late\",\"id\":\"LATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who only got it because of the instrument or the cutoff, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Local average treatment effect\"},{\"acronym\":\"CACE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.cace\",\"id\":\"CACE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For the people who comply with what they were offered, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Complier average causal effect\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.weak_robust\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\",\"some of the robustness probes it names have no card of their own yet\"],\"id\":\"iv.weak_robust\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Report the set of effects the data cannot reject, which stays honest however weak the instrument is.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"auto\",\"robust\",\"classical\",\"cluster\"],\"default\":\"auto\",\"help\":\"'auto' uses cluster-robust standard errors when a clustering unit is set, and heteroskedasticity-robust ones otherwise.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"se_type\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Relabels the estimate an average treatment effect. This is an assertion about the world, not a setting: without it the number is a LATE for the units the instrument moved.\",\"label\":\"Assert one effect for everyone\",\"name\":\"assume_homogeneous_effects\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"Applies to the Wald interval and to the robust set alike.\",\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.9999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Each one gets a placebo reduced form. It can catch the exclusion restriction failing; nothing can confirm it.\",\"label\":\"Outcomes the instrument should not move\",\"name\":\"placebo_outcomes\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Every extra endogenous variable needs its own excluded instrument.\",\"label\":\"Further endogenous variables\",\"name\":\"extra_endogenous\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":201,\"help\":\"The Anderson-Rubin set is found by inverting the test on this grid, then refining the edges by bisection.\",\"label\":\"Grid points for the robust set\",\"max\":2001,\"min\":51,\"name\":\"grid_points\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":8.0,\"help\":\"Widened automatically when the set has not closed by the edge.\",\"label\":\"Grid half-width (in standard errors)\",\"max\":500.0,\"min\":1.0,\"name\":\"grid_span\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"2sls\",\"liml\"],\"default\":\"2sls\",\"help\":\"Only a reference point. The set is the result; with a weak instrument no point estimate is trustworthy.\",\"label\":\"Point estimate shown beside the set\",\"name\":\"point_estimator\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Moreira's CLR set is usually shorter than Anderson-Rubin when the instruments are strong. It is drawn only with several instruments and without clustering, because that is where the form used here is reliable.\",\"label\":\"Also draw the conditional likelihood ratio set\",\"name\":\"include_clr\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":4000,\"help\":\"The conditional distribution is simulated; more draws mean smoother edges.\",\"label\":\"Simulation draws for the CLR set\",\"max\":200000,\"min\":500,\"name\":\"clr_draws\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"}],\"plain_language\":\"Report the set of effects the data cannot reject, which stays honest however weak the instrument is.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.subset\",\"id\":\"probe.subset\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Re-estimate on random subsets. The answer should move about as much as losing that much data costs, and no more.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.subset\",\"title\":\"Subset stability\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"id\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Add a variable that causes nothing to the adjustment set. The estimate should barely move.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"title\":\"Random common cause\"},{\"explain_key\":null,\"id\":\"probe.leave_one_instrument_out\",\"in_catalogue\":false,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":null,\"requested_as\":\"probe.leave_one_instrument_out\",\"title\":\"Leave one instrument out\"}],\"references\":[\"Anderson & Rubin (1949), Estimation of the parameters of a single equation\",\"Moreira (2003), A conditional likelihood ratio test for structural models\",\"Montiel Olea & Pflueger (2013), A robust test for weak instruments\",\"Andrews, Stock & Sun (2019), Weak instruments in IV regression: theory and practice\",\"Lee, McCrary, Moreira & Porter (2022), Valid t-ratio inference for IV\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"at least one measured confounder\",\"a clustering variable\",\"weight\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\",\"an instrument\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.iv\",\"id\":\"iv\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"An instrument or encouragement changed treatment, not the outcome directly.\",\"title\":\"Something else pushed people in\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.2sls\",\"id\":\"iv.2sls\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Use only the part of the treatment that the instrument moved, and see what happened to the outcome.\",\"title\":\"Two-stage least squares\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.gmm\",\"id\":\"iv.gmm\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Weight the instruments by how informative each one actually is, using a weight matrix estimated from the data.\",\"title\":\"Two-step GMM\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.liml\",\"id\":\"iv.liml\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"The maximum-likelihood cousin of two-stage least squares, which stays much better behaved when the instruments are weak.\",\"title\":\"LIML (and Fuller)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.mte\",\"id\":\"iv.mte\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Trace the effect as a function of how reluctant a unit is to be treated, instead of reporting one local average.\",\"title\":\"Marginal treatment effects\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.shift_share\",\"id\":\"iv.shift_share\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Combine national shocks with local exposure shares to build an instrument for local changes.\",\"title\":\"Shift-share (Bartik) instruments\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"Something else pushed people in\",\"LATE\",\"CACE\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Weak-instrument-robust confidence set\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.relevance\",\"explains\":\"The instrument actually moves treatment, and moves it enough that the resulting estimate is not mostly noise.\",\"id\":\"relevance\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Instrument relevance\",\"worry_when\":\"An effective F below about 10; a first-stage coefficient that is substantively tiny even if statistically significant; many instruments.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exclusion\",\"explains\":\"The instrument affects the outcome only through the treatment. On the board, that is the arrow you did not draw.\",\"id\":\"exclusion\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exclusion restriction\",\"worry_when\":\"The instrument is a policy that changed several things at once; it is correlated with geography, time or institutions that have their own effects; it was chosen because it predicted the outcome.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.monotonicity\",\"explains\":\"The instrument pushes everyone the same way, or not at all. Nobody takes the treatment only because they were discouraged from it.\",\"id\":\"monotonicity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Monotonicity / no defiers\",\"worry_when\":\"The instrument is an incentive that could plausibly backfire for some people, or it is a judge or examiner whose leniency ordering differs across case types.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"Exclusion is untestable and usually the weakest link: if the instrument reaches the outcome by any other route, the bias is the violation divided by the first stage, which is enormous when the instrument is weak. The set can be unbounded or empty, which people read as a bug: unbounded means the data cannot rule out large effects, and empty means the instruments contradict each other.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"Its coverage does not depend on the first stage being strong. When the instrument is weak this is the only interval on the screen that means what it says, and an unbounded set is a real answer, not a failure.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\",\"some of the robustness probes it names have no card of their own yet\"],\"id\":\"iv.weak_robust\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"iv.weak_robust\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"iv\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"first_stage\",\"reduced_form\",\"overid\",\"weak_iv_set\",\"endogeneity\",\"compliers\",\"placebo_reduced_form\"],\"disrecommend_when\":null,\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"ivmodel\"},\"estimands\":[\"LATE\",\"CACE\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.iv.weak_robust\",\"id\":\"iv.weak_robust\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\",\"linearmodels\"],\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Report the set of effects the data cannot reject, which stays honest however weak the instrument is.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"auto\",\"robust\",\"classical\",\"cluster\"],\"default\":\"auto\",\"help\":\"'auto' uses cluster-robust standard errors when a clustering unit is set, and heteroskedasticity-robust ones otherwise.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"se_type\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Relabels the estimate an average treatment effect. This is an assertion about the world, not a setting: without it the number is a LATE for the units the instrument moved.\",\"label\":\"Assert one effect for everyone\",\"name\":\"assume_homogeneous_effects\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"Applies to the Wald interval and to the robust set alike.\",\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.9999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Each one gets a placebo reduced form. It can catch the exclusion restriction failing; nothing can confirm it.\",\"label\":\"Outcomes the instrument should not move\",\"name\":\"placebo_outcomes\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Every extra endogenous variable needs its own excluded instrument.\",\"label\":\"Further endogenous variables\",\"name\":\"extra_endogenous\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":201,\"help\":\"The Anderson-Rubin set is found by inverting the test on this grid, then refining the edges by bisection.\",\"label\":\"Grid points for the robust set\",\"max\":2001,\"min\":51,\"name\":\"grid_points\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":8.0,\"help\":\"Widened automatically when the set has not closed by the edge.\",\"label\":\"Grid half-width (in standard errors)\",\"max\":500.0,\"min\":1.0,\"name\":\"grid_span\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"2sls\",\"liml\"],\"default\":\"2sls\",\"help\":\"Only a reference point. The set is the result; with a weak instrument no point estimate is trustworthy.\",\"label\":\"Point estimate shown beside the set\",\"name\":\"point_estimator\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Moreira's CLR set is usually shorter than Anderson-Rubin when the instruments are strong. It is drawn only with several instruments and without clustering, because that is where the form used here is reliable.\",\"label\":\"Also draw the conditional likelihood ratio set\",\"name\":\"include_clr\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":4000,\"help\":\"The conditional distribution is simulated; more draws mean smoother edges.\",\"label\":\"Simulation draws for the CLR set\",\"max\":200000,\"min\":500,\"name\":\"clr_draws\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"}],\"probes\":[\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"probe.subset\",\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"probe.leave_one_instrument_out\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1214/aoms/1177730090\",\"requested_as\":\"Anderson & Rubin (1949), Estimation of the parameters of a single equation\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1111/1468-0262.00438\",\"requested_as\":\"Moreira (2003), A conditional likelihood ratio test for structural models\"},{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:df637410f69a1d8930a5\",\"requested_as\":\"Montiel Olea & Pflueger (2013), A robust test for weak instruments\"},{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:4eccf47fd5ff40c6c9f1\",\"requested_as\":\"Andrews, Stock & Sun (2019), Weak instruments in IV regression: theory and practice\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1257/aer.20211063\",\"requested_as\":\"Lee, McCrary, Moreira & Porter (2022), Valid t-ratio inference for IV\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"10.1214/aoms/1177730090\",\"10.1111/1468-0262.00438\",\"source:unresolved:df637410f69a1d8930a5\",\"source:unresolved:4eccf47fd5ff40c6c9f1\",\"10.1257/aer.20211063\"],\"references\":[\"Anderson & Rubin (1949), Estimation of the parameters of a single equation\",\"Moreira (2003), A conditional likelihood ratio test for structural models\",\"Montiel Olea & Pflueger (2013), A robust test for weak instruments\",\"Andrews, Stock & Sun (2019), Weak instruments in IV regression: theory and practice\",\"Lee, McCrary, Moreira & Porter (2022), Valid t-ratio inference for IV\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"confounders\",\"cluster\",\"weight\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"outcome\",\"instruments\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/iv.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"ab0a0614687ffe9aa5d99f36252cc388ee4436f7f45bc43e98bbed8df9e4bb64\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Weak-instrument-robust confidence set\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"Exclusion is untestable and usually the weakest link: if the instrument reaches the outcome by any other route, the bias is the violation divided by the first stage, which is enormous when the instrument is weak. The set can be unbounded or empty, which people read as a bug: unbounded means the data cannot rule out large effects, and empty means the instruments contradict each other.\",\"why_recommended\":\"Its coverage does not depend on the first stage being strong. When the instrument is weak this is the only interval on the screen that means what it says, and an unbounded set is a real answer, not a failure.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:02d72b32732d1a4e73259959\",\"object_id\":\"design:iv\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"iv.weak_robust\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:0e70e26fb9f98ae247c3f867\",\"object_id\":\"diagnostic:endogeneity\",\"predicate\":\"checked_by_diagnostic\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"iv.weak_robust\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:12140c274603615ff9f4349f\",\"object_id\":\"iv.2sls\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model