 does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:f63888f3616fcaa6d0cc86a0\",\"object_id\":\"concept:dynamic-regime\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:robins2000\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"long.lmtp\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:fe5d4fb4a1833cb86f5e6ca6\",\"object_id\":\"concept:causal-framing\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:pearl2009\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"long.lmtp\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Estimate the effect of shifting a continuous or multi-valued treatment, rather than of setting everyone to one value.\",\"title\":\"Longitudinal modified treatment policies (lmtp)\"}" .
<urn:capy:long.ltmle> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Sequential doubly robust (ICE g-formula with augmentation)" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:long.ltmle\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:long.ltmle\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1515/1557-4679.1370\",\"bang2005\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"ltmle\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"ltmle\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.longitudinal\",\"id\":\"longitudinal\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"The same person is treated, untreated, treated again; confounders also move.\",\"title\":\"Treatment that changes over time\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.temporal_ordering\",\"id\":\"temporal_ordering\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Temporal ordering of covariates\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.person_time\",\"id\":\"person_time\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Person-time and switching\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.positivity_by_period\",\"id\":\"positivity_by_period\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Positivity by period\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.regime_support\",\"id\":\"regime_support\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Support for the intervention regime\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.augmentation_gap\",\"id\":\"augmentation_gap\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Augmentation gap\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.influence_spread\",\"id\":\"influence_spread\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Influence-function spread\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"ATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.ate\",\"id\":\"ATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"If everyone got the programme, how would the average outcome change?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.long.ltmle\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"long.ltmle\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Regress backwards from the final outcome, then correct with the treatment probabilities: right if either set of models is right.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\",\"threshold\"],\"default\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\"],\"help\":\"Static rules, or a rule that starts treatment when a covariate crosses a line. The natural course is what the data already shows, so it is not an option here.\",\"label\":\"Strategies to compare\",\"name\":\"interventions\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"multiselect\"},{\"choices\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\",\"threshold\"],\"default\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\"],\"label\":\"Headline comparison\",\"name\":\"contrast\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"multiselect\"},{\"choices\":[\"markov\",\"full\"],\"default\":\"markov\",\"help\":\"'markov' uses this period and the last; 'full' uses everything measured so far, which needs a lot more data.\",\"label\":\"How much history each regression sees\",\"name\":\"history\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":0.01,\"help\":\"Bounds the correction term. Reported, never silent.\",\"label\":\"Floor on the probability of following the strategy\",\"max\":0.2,\"min\":0.001,\"name\":\"g_bound\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Threshold rule: variable\",\"name\":\"threshold_variable\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"column\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Threshold rule: value\",\"name\":\"threshold_value\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"plain_language\":\"Regress backwards from the final outcome, then correct with the treatment probabilities: right if either set of models is right.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.subset\",\"id\":\"probe.subset\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Re-estimate on random subsets. The answer should move about as much as losing that much data costs, and no more.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.subset\",\"title\":\"Subset stability\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"id\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Add a variable that causes nothing to the adjustment set. The estimate should barely move.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"title\":\"Random common cause\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"}],\"references\":[\"Bang & Robins (2005), Doubly robust estimation in missing data and causal inference models\",\"van der Laan & Gruber (2012), Targeted minimum loss based estimation of causal effects of multiple time point interventions\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"strata\",\"weight\",\"a clustering variable\",\"censoring\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a unit id\",\"a time variable\",\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\",\"at least one measured confounder\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.longitudinal\",\"id\":\"longitudinal\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"The same person is treated, untreated, treated again; confounders also move.\",\"title\":\"Treatment that changes over time\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.long.g_estimation\",\"id\":\"long.g_estimation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Estimate the effect of a treatment regime by finding the parameter that removes the association between treatment and the blipped-down outcome.\",\"title\":\"G-estimation of structural nested models\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.long.gformula\",\"id\":\"long.gformula\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Model each period in turn, then simulate the world where everyone followed the strategy you name.\",\"title\":\"Parametric g-formula\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.long.lmtp\",\"id\":\"long.lmtp\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Estimate the effect of shifting a continuous or multi-valued treatment, rather than of setting everyone to one value.\",\"title\":\"Longitudinal modified treatment policies (lmtp)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.long.ltmle_survival\",\"id\":\"long.ltmle_survival\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Time-to-event outcomes with time-varying treatment and censoring, targeted at each time.\",\"title\":\"Longitudinal TMLE for survival outcomes\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.long.msm_iptw\",\"id\":\"long.msm_iptw\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Reweight each person-period so the treated and untreated histories look alike, then fit one simple model to the reweighted data.\",\"title\":\"Marginal structural model (time-varying weights)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.obs.missing.mice\",\"id\":\"obs.missing.mice\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Impute the missing values several times, run the analysis in each, and combine -- instead of dropping every row with a gap.\",\"title\":\"Multiple imputation compatible with the analysis\"}],\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"status_label\":\"Reasonable\",\"tags\":[\"Treatment that changes over time\",\"ATE\",\"Reasonable\"],\"title\":\"Sequential doubly robust (ICE g-formula with augmentation)\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.no_time_varying_confounding\",\"explains\":\"At every period, the things that drive the treatment decision and also affect the outcome are measured -- and measured before that decision.\",\"id\":\"no_time_varying_confounding\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No unmeasured time-varying confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Clinical measurements taken after the dose was changed; employment status recorded at the end of a period used to explain treatment at its start.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.positivity\",\"explains\":\"Every kind of unit had some chance of being treated and some chance of not being treated. Where that fails, there is no comparison to make and the model is inventing one.\",\"id\":\"positivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Positivity / overlap\",\"worry_when\":\"Any single weight carries a large share of the total; the effective sample is far below the nominal one; the propensity model separates the arms almost perfectly; treated units sit outside the control group's range.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sequential_ignorability\",\"explains\":\"No unmeasured confounding of the treatment-outcome relationship, and none of the mediator-outcome relationship either, even after conditioning on treatment.\",\"id\":\"sequential_ignorability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Sequential ignorability\",\"worry_when\":\"There is a variable affected by treatment that also confounds the mediator-outcome relationship. Under that structure the natural effects are not identified at all.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"This is the sequential doubly robust estimator, not targeted maximum likelihood: without the targeting step nothing forces the answer inside the outcome's own range, which is why every run is marked provisional. When almost nobody follows the strategy, the correction term divides by a tiny probability and the interval widens accordingly.\",\"When a substitution estimator is required (bounded outcomes, rare events); use R's ltmle until the targeting step lands here\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"Two chances to be right -- the outcome regressions or the treatment models -- and a standard error that comes from the estimator's own influence function rather than a resampling loop.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"long.ltmle\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"long.ltmle\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"longitudinal\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"temporal_ordering\",\"person_time\",\"positivity_by_period\",\"regime_support\",\"augmentation_gap\",\"influence_spread\"],\"disrecommend_when\":\"When a substitution estimator is required (bounded outcomes, rare events); use R's ltmle until the targeting step lands here\",\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"ltmle\"},\"estimands\":[\"ATE\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.long.ltmle\",\"id\":\"long.ltmle\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\"],\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Regress backwards from the final outcome, then correct with the treatment probabilities: right if either set of models is right.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\",\"threshold\"],\"default\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\"],\"help\":\"Static rules, or a rule that starts treatment when a covariate crosses a line. The natural course is what the data already shows, so it is not an option here.\",\"label\":\"Strategies to compare\",\"name\":\"interventions\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"multiselect\"},{\"choices\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\",\"threshold\"],\"default\":[\"treat_all\",\"treat_none\"],\"label\":\"Headline comparison\",\"name\":\"contrast\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"multiselect\"},{\"choices\":[\"markov\",\"full\"],\"default\":\"markov\",\"help\":\"'markov' uses this period and the last; 'full' uses everything measured so far, which needs a lot more data.\",\"label\":\"How much history each regression sees\",\"name\":\"history\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":0.01,\"help\":\"Bounds the correction term. Reported, never silent.\",\"label\":\"Floor on the probability of following the strategy\",\"max\":0.2,\"min\":0.001,\"name\":\"g_bound\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Threshold rule: variable\",\"name\":\"threshold_variable\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"column\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Threshold rule: value\",\"name\":\"threshold_value\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"probes\":[\"probe.subset\",\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"probe.alternate_spec\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"bang2005\",\"requested_as\":\"Bang & Robins (2005), Doubly robust estimation in missing data and causal inference models\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1515/1557-4679.1370\",\"requested_as\":\"van der Laan & Gruber (2012), Targeted minimum loss based estimation of causal effects of multiple time point interventions\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"bang2005\",\"10.1515/1557-4679.1370\"],\"references\":[\"Bang & Robins (2005), Doubly robust estimation in missing data and causal inference models\",\"van der Laan & Gruber (2012), Targeted minimum loss based estimation of causal effects of multiple time point interventions\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"strata\",\"weight\",\"cluster\",\"censoring\"],\"roles_required\":[\"unit\",\"time\",\"treatment\",\"outcome\",\"confounders\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/longitudinal.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"49a2064131adc4f82db0de13c3127729b10c3407c6c933d1afed97a11dce4e83\",\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"title\":\"Sequential doubly robust (ICE g-formula with augmentation)\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"This is the sequential doubly robust estimator, not targeted maximum likelihood: without the targeting step nothing forces the answer inside the outcome's own range, which is why every run is marked provisional. When almost nobody follows the strategy, the correction term divides by a tiny probability and the interval widens accordingly.\",\"why_recommended\":\"Two chances to be right -- the outcome regressions or the treatment models -- and a standard error that comes from the estimator's own influence function rather than a resampling loop.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:013ecd095b5c4efef9e0df48\",\"object_id\":\"assumption:sequential_ignorability\",\"predicate\":\"requires_assumption\",\"provenance\":[