d primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"obs.matching.optimal\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Choose the whole set of matches at once to minimise total distance, rather than greedily one treated unit at a time.\",\"title\":\"Optimal and full matching\"}" .
<urn:capy:obs.missing.mice> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Multiple imputation compatible with the analysis" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:obs.missing.mice\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:obs.missing.mice\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1201/9780429492259\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":\"Not wrapped. Today every dropped row appears in the sample flow with its reason.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":false,\"r\":\"mice\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"mice\",\"MatchThem\"],\"runs_here\":false,\"summary\":\"Not built into the app yet. The authoritative version is the R package mice, which the Engines screen can install for you.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"},{\"explain_key\":\"design.did\",\"id\":\"did\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Some places or groups got it earlier than others.\",\"title\":\"Policy rolled out over time\"},{\"explain_key\":\"design.longitudinal\",\"id\":\"longitudinal\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"The same person is treated, untreated, treated again; confounders also move.\",\"title\":\"Treatment that changes over time\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.outcome_distribution\",\"id\":\"outcome_distribution\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Outcome distribution\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"ATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.ate\",\"id\":\"ATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"If everyone got the programme, how would the average outcome change?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect\"},{\"acronym\":\"ATT\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.att\",\"id\":\"ATT\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who actually got it, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect on the treated\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.obs.missing.mice\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"obs.missing.mice\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Impute the missing values several times, run the analysis in each, and combine -- instead of dropping every row with a gap.\",\"options\":[],\"plain_language\":\"Impute the missing values several times, run the analysis in each, and combine -- instead of dropping every row with a gap.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.subset\",\"id\":\"probe.subset\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Re-estimate on random subsets. The answer should move about as much as losing that much data costs, and no more.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.subset\",\"title\":\"Subset stability\"}],\"references\":[\"van Buuren (2018), Flexible Imputation of Missing Data\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[],\"roles_optional\":[],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"},{\"explain_key\":\"design.did\",\"id\":\"did\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Some places or groups got it earlier than others.\",\"title\":\"Policy rolled out over time\"},{\"explain_key\":\"design.longitudinal\",\"id\":\"longitudinal\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"The same person is treated, untreated, treated again; confounders also move.\",\"title\":\"Treatment that changes over time\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.bounds.manski\",\"id\":\"bounds.manski\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Report the range the effect must lie in given only what the data can support, without assuming away the missing counterfactual.\",\"title\":\"Manski bounds\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.bjs_imputation\",\"id\":\"did.bjs_imputation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Learn what untreated life looks like from untreated cells only, then ask how far each treated cell landed from it.\",\"title\":\"Imputation (Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.callaway_santanna\",\"id\":\"did.callaway_santanna\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Estimate one clean before-and-after for every adoption cohort, then say out loud how you averaged them.\",\"title\":\"Callaway & Sant'Anna group-time effects\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.chaisemartin\",\"id\":\"did.chaisemartin\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"An estimator built for panels where treatment switches on and off, which the imputation and cohort estimators assume never happens.\",\"title\":\"de Chaisemartin & D'Haultfoeuille\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.dr_did\",\"id\":\"did.dr_did\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"One before-and-after with covariates, using an outcome model and a comparison-group model together so either one can carry it.\",\"title\":\"Doubly robust DiD\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.event_study\",\"id\":\"did.event_study\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Plot the effect period by period around adoption, so you can see whether the gap opened when the policy arrived or long before it.\",\"title\":\"Event study (leads and lags)\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"Adjust for background differences\",\"Policy rolled out over time\",\"Treatment that changes over time\",\"ATE\",\"ATT\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Multiple imputation compatible with the analysis\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exchangeability\",\"explains\":\"Treated and untreated units are comparable once you condition on the confounders you measured. Everything that pushed people towards treatment and also moves the outcome is in your adjustment set.\",\"id\":\"exchangeability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exchangeability / no unmeasured confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Treatment was chosen by people who knew something about the likely outcome that you do not observe. Clinical judgement, self-selection into a programme, and administrative triage are the classic cases.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.positivity\",\"explains\":\"Every kind of unit had some chance of being treated and some chance of not being treated. Where that fails, there is no comparison to make and the model is inventing one.\",\"id\":\"positivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Positivity / overlap\",\"worry_when\":\"Any single weight carries a large share of the total; the effective sample is far below the nominal one; the propensity model separates the arms almost perfectly; treated units sit outside the control group's range.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.parallel_trends\",\"explains\":\"Without the policy, treated and comparison groups would have moved the same way. Not that they were at the same level -- that their paths would have been parallel.\",\"id\":\"parallel_trends\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Parallel trends\",\"worry_when\":\"Pre-period event-study coefficients drift away from zero; the policy was adopted because outcomes were already moving; the groups differ in composition in ways that interact with time.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.no_anticipation\",\"explains\":\"Units did not change behaviour before treatment arrived because they knew it was coming.\",\"id\":\"no_anticipation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No anticipation\",\"worry_when\":\"There was a public announcement well before the policy started, or the pre-period coefficients move in the period immediately before adoption.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.no_time_varying_confounding\",\"explains\":\"At every period, the things that drive the treatment decision and also affect the outcome are measured -- and measured before that decision.\",\"id\":\"no_time_varying_confounding\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No unmeasured time-varying confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Clinical measurements taken after the dose was changed; employment status recorded at the end of a period used to explain treatment at its start.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sequential_ignorability\",\"explains\":\"No unmeasured confounding of the treatment-outcome relationship, and none of the mediator-outcome relationship either, even after conditioning on treatment.\",\"id\":\"sequential_ignorability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Sequential ignorability\",\"worry_when\":\"There is a variable affected by treatment that also confounds the mediator-outcome relationship. Under that structure the natural effects are not identified at all.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"The imputation model has to be compatible with the analysis model, including its interactions; imputing the outcome and then matching on it is a common and serious error.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"Complete-case analysis is unbiased only under strong conditions, and this product logs how many rows it costs you on every run. Imputation uses them instead.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"obs.missing.mice\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"obs.missing.mice\",\"registry\":{\"coming\":\"Not wrapped. Today every dropped row appears in the sample flow with its reason.\",\"designs\":[\"observational\",\"did\",\"longitudinal\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"outcome_distribution\"],\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":false,\"r\":\"mice\"},\"estimands\":[\"ATE\",\"ATT\"],\"id\":\"obs.missing.mice\",\"one_liner\":\"Impute the missing values several times, run the analysis in each, and combine -- instead of dropping every row with a gap.\",\"probes\":[\"probe.subset\"],\"r_needs\":[\"mice\",\"MatchThem\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1201/9780429492259\",\"requested_as\":\"van Buuren (2018), Flexible Imputation of Missing Data\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"10.1201/9780429492259\"],\"references\":[\"van Buuren (2018), Flexible Imputation of Missing Data\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"outcome\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/registry/methods.extra.yaml\",\"source_sha256\":\"2cb349e9f7f7e6f88c10c18d81478656fd420eda7ca977d9767610ac8c7a4be0\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Multiple imputation compatible with the analysis\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"The imputation model has to be compatible with the analysis model, including its interactions; imputing the outcome and then matching on it is a common and serious error.\",\"why_recommended\":\"Complete-case analysis is unbiased only under strong conditions, and this product logs how many rows it costs you on every run. Imputation uses them instead.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:0406fe6f9ae4c35aa7869b5e\",\"object_id\":\"assumption:positivity\",\"predicate\":\"requires_assumption\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"obs.missing.mice\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:06bb1026888e30e6092b80d5\",\"object_id\":\"concept:causal-framing\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:pearl2009\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original ex