iginal or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"obs.missing.mice\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:e8c19103e9d95345a2d86a43\",\"object_id\":\"concept:collider\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:pearl2009\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"obs.missing.mice\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:ef76d75e91cad6cf37652d80\",\"object_id\":\"estimand:ATT\",\"predicate\":\"targets_estimand\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"obs.missing.mice\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Impute the missing values several times, run the analysis in each, and combine -- instead of dropping every row with a gap.\",\"title\":\"Multiple imputation compatible with the analysis\"}" .
<urn:capy:obs.outcome_regression> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Outcome regression (g-computation)" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:obs.outcome_regression\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:obs.outcome_regression\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1016/0270-0255(86)90088-6\",\"hernan2020\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"marginaleffects\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"marginaleffects\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.love\",\"id\":\"love\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Covariate balance (Love plot)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.model_reliance\",\"id\":\"model_reliance\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"How much the model is doing\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"ATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.ate\",\"id\":\"ATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"If everyone got the programme, how would the average outcome change?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect\"},{\"acronym\":\"ATT\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.att\",\"id\":\"ATT\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who actually got it, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect on the treated\"},{\"acronym\":\"ATC\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.atc\",\"id\":\"ATC\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who didn't get it, what would it have done?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect on the controls\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.obs.outcome_regression\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"obs.outcome_regression\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Model the outcome, then ask what would have happened if everyone had been treated, and if nobody had.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Interacts the treatment with every covariate, so the model does not force one effect on everyone.\",\"label\":\"Let the effect vary with covariates\",\"name\":\"interactions\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"HC1\",\"HC3\",\"classical\"],\"default\":\"HC1\",\"help\":\"HC3 is safer in small samples.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"vcov\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":400,\"help\":\"Used when the contrast is not a single coefficient.\",\"label\":\"Bootstrap draws\",\"max\":5000,\"min\":50,\"name\":\"bootstrap_reps\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"}],\"plain_language\":\"Model the outcome, then ask what would have happened if everyone had been treated, and if nobody had.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.subset\",\"id\":\"probe.subset\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Re-estimate on random subsets. The answer should move about as much as losing that much data costs, and no more.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.subset\",\"title\":\"Subset stability\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"id\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Add a variable that causes nothing to the adjustment set. The estimate should barely move.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"title\":\"Random common cause\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.cinelli_hazlett\",\"id\":\"probe.cinelli_hazlett\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"How strong would an unmeasured confounder have to be -- compared with the covariates you already have -- to explain the estimate away?\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.cinelli_hazlett\",\"title\":\"Cinelli-Hazlett sensitivity (partial R2)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"}],\"references\":[\"Robins (1986), A new approach to causal inference in mortality studies\",\"Hernán & Robins (2020), Causal Inference: What If, ch. 13\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"a clustering variable\",\"weight\",\"effect_modifiers\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.bounds.manski\",\"id\":\"bounds.manski\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Report the range the effect must lie in given only what the data can support, without assuming away the missing counterfactual.\",\"title\":\"Manski bounds\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.interference.exposure\",\"id\":\"interference.exposure\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"When one unit's treatment affects another's outcome, estimate the direct and spillover effects separately instead of pretending neither exists.\",\"title\":\"Interference and spillovers\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.causal_forest\",\"id\":\"ml.causal_forest\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Grow trees that look for units whose effect differs, keeping the rows that chose each split away from the rows that estimate it.\",\"title\":\"Honest causal forest\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.dml_irm\",\"id\":\"ml.dml_irm\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"A separate outcome model for each arm plus a treatment model, combined in a doubly robust score: right if either side is right.\",\"title\":\"Double ML (interactive)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.dml_plr\",\"id\":\"ml.dml_plr\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Predict the outcome and the treatment from the confounders, then regress what is left of one on what is left of the other.\",\"title\":\"Double ML (partially linear)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.metalearner\",\"id\":\"ml.metalearner\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Build the per-unit effect out of ordinary prediction models, four different ways, on the same cross-fitting.\",\"title\":\"Meta-learner (T, S, X, DR)\"}],\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"status_label\":\"Reasonable\",\"tags\":[\"Adjust for background differences\",\"ATE\",\"ATT\",\"ATC\",\"Reasonable\"],\"title\":\"Outcome regression (g-computation)\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exchangeability\",\"explains\":\"Treated and untreated units are comparable once you condition on the confounders you measured. Everything that pushed people towards treatment and also moves the outcome is in your adjustment set.\",\"id\":\"exchangeability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exchangeability / no unmeasured confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Treatment was chosen by people who knew something about the likely outcome that you do not observe. Clinical judgement, self-selection into a programme, and administrative triage are the classic cases.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.positivity\",\"explains\":\"Every kind of unit had some chance of being treated and some chance of not being treated. Where that fails, there is no comparison to make and the model is inventing one.\",\"id\":\"positivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Positivity / overlap\",\"worry_when\":\"Any single weight carries a large share of the total; the effective sample is far below the nominal one; the propensity model separates the arms almost perfectly; treated units sit outside the control group's range.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"It extrapolates silently. Where treated and untreated units do not overlap, the model invents the comparison and nothing in the output tells you.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"Simple, transparent, and the natural baseline when the covariates are few and the groups genuinely overlap.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"obs.outcome_regression\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"obs.outcome_regression\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"observational\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"love\",\"model_reliance\"],\"disrecommend_when\":null,\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"marginaleffects\"},\"estimands\":[\"ATE\",\"ATT\",\"ATC\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.obs.outcome_regression\",\"id\":\"obs.outcome_regression\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\"],\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Model the outcome, then ask what would have happened if everyone had been treated, and if nobody had.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Interacts the treatment with every covariate, so the model does not force one effect on everyone.\",\"label\":\"Let the effect vary with covariates\",\"name\":\"interactions\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"HC1\",\"HC3\",\"classical\"],\"default\":\"HC1\",\"help\":\"HC3 is safer in small samples.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"vcov\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":400,\"help\":\"Used when the contrast is not a single coefficient.\",\"label\":\"Bootstrap draws\",\"max\":5000,\"min\":50,\"name\":\"bootstrap_reps\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"}],\"probes\":[\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"probe.subset\",\"probe.random_common_cause\",\"probe.cinelli_hazlett\",\"probe.alternate_spec\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1016/0270-0255(86)90088-6\",\"requested_as\":\"Robins (1986), A new approach to causal inference in mortality studies\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"hernan2020\",\"requested_as\":\"Hernán & Robins (2020), Causal Inference: What If, ch. 13\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"10.1016/0270-0255(86)90088-6\",\"hernan2020\"],\"references\":[\"Robins (1986), A new approach to causal inference in mortality studies\",\"Hernán & Robins (2020), Causal Inference: What If, ch. 13\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"cluster\",\"weight\",\"effect_modifiers\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"outcome\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/observational.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"f9dfafacc9dacabf923e4d48367973338dbe326bdf5c222ade0dedf0470b5ccb\",\"status\":\"reasonable\",\"title\":\"Outcome regression (g-computation)\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"It extrapolates silently. Where treated and untreated units do not overlap, the model invents the comparison and nothing in the output tells you.\",\"why_recommended\":\"Simple, transparent, and the natural baseline when the covariates are few and the groups genuinely overlap.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:0d29a71dcfdbbf97b76195a1\",\"object_id\":\"concept:standardization\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"hernan2020\",\"source:ontology:cole2004\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":