aterial; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"probe.random_common_cause\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:ff30a9b5e0cc449ceaca6c70\",\"object_id\":\"design:rd\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"probe.random_common_cause\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Add a variable that causes nothing to the adjustment set. The estimate should barely move.\",\"title\":\"Random common cause\"}" .
<urn:capy:probe.rosenbaum> a capy:probe ; skos:prefLabel "Rosenbaum bounds" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"probe:probe.rosenbaum\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"probe:probe.rosenbaum\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1007/978-1-4419-1213-8\",\"source:unresolved:a1f7672f4e91623cf9ed\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"rbounds\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"rbounds\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.rosenbaum_bounds\",\"id\":\"rosenbaum_bounds\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Rosenbaum bounds\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.pair_quality\",\"id\":\"pair_quality\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Matched-pair quality\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"ATT\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.att\",\"id\":\"ATT\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who actually got it, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect on the treated\"}],\"explain_key\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"How unequal could the odds of treatment be inside a matched pair before the conclusion stopped being clear?\",\"options\":[{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The number this probe is about. Filled in automatically when the probe is launched from a result.\",\"label\":\"Parent estimate\",\"name\":\"parent_estimate\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Used to place the parent's confidence interval on the same scale.\",\"label\":\"Parent standard error\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"parent_se\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Which analysis this probe is attached to. Some probes re-run it to get the fitted model rather than just the number.\",\"label\":\"Parent method\",\"name\":\"parent_method\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":3.0,\"help\":\"Gamma is the ratio of treatment odds between two matched units.\",\"label\":\"Largest Gamma to try\",\"max\":20.0,\"min\":1.1,\"name\":\"gamma_max\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.1,\"label\":\"Step\",\"max\":1.0,\"min\":0.01,\"name\":\"gamma_step\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.05,\"label\":\"Level the conclusion is judged at\",\"max\":0.5,\"min\":0.001,\"name\":\"alpha\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"two-sided\",\"greater\",\"less\"],\"default\":\"two-sided\",\"label\":\"Alternative\",\"name\":\"alternative\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"choices\":[\"logit_ps\",\"ps\",\"mahalanobis\"],\"default\":\"logit_ps\",\"help\":\"How the probe forms the 1:1 pairs it bounds.\",\"label\":\"Pair on\",\"name\":\"distance\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Caliper (SD of the score)\",\"max\":2.0,\"min\":0.01,\"name\":\"caliper\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"plain_language\":\"How unequal could the odds of treatment be inside a matched pair before the conclusion stopped being clear?\",\"probes\":[],\"references\":[\"Rosenbaum (2002), Observational Studies, 2nd ed., chapter 4\",\"Rosenbaum (2010), Design of Observational Studies\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"a clustering variable\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"an outcome\",\"at least one measured confounder\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.observational\",\"id\":\"observational\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Treatment was not random; we can measure the things that made people get it.\",\"title\":\"Adjust for background differences\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.bounds.manski\",\"id\":\"bounds.manski\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Report the range the effect must lie in given only what the data can support, without assuming away the missing counterfactual.\",\"title\":\"Manski bounds\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.interference.exposure\",\"id\":\"interference.exposure\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"When one unit's treatment affects another's outcome, estimate the direct and spillover effects separately instead of pretending neither exists.\",\"title\":\"Interference and spillovers\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.causal_forest\",\"id\":\"ml.causal_forest\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Grow trees that look for units whose effect differs, keeping the rows that chose each split away from the rows that estimate it.\",\"title\":\"Honest causal forest\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.dml_irm\",\"id\":\"ml.dml_irm\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"A separate outcome model for each arm plus a treatment model, combined in a doubly robust score: right if either side is right.\",\"title\":\"Double ML (interactive)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.ml.metalearner\",\"id\":\"ml.metalearner\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Build the per-unit effect out of ordinary prediction models, four different ways, on the same cross-fitting.\",\"title\":\"Meta-learner (T, S, X, DR)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.obs.aipw\",\"id\":\"obs.aipw\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Use a treatment model and an outcome model together; it is right if either one is.\",\"title\":\"Doubly robust (AIPW)\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"Adjust for background differences\",\"ATT\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Rosenbaum bounds\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exchangeability\",\"explains\":\"Treated and untreated units are comparable once you condition on the confounders you measured. Everything that pushed people towards treatment and also moves the outcome is in your adjustment set.\",\"id\":\"exchangeability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exchangeability / no unmeasured confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Treatment was chosen by people who knew something about the likely outcome that you do not observe. Clinical judgement, self-selection into a programme, and administrative triage are the classic cases.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.positivity\",\"explains\":\"Every kind of unit had some chance of being treated and some chance of not being treated. Where that fails, there is no comparison to make and the model is inventing one.\",\"id\":\"positivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Positivity / overlap\",\"worry_when\":\"Any single weight carries a large share of the total; the effective sample is far below the nominal one; the propensity model separates the arms almost perfectly; treated units sit outside the control group's range.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"It bounds bias that operates *within* pairs, and it tests the sharp null of no effect for anybody. The pairs it bounds are the ones it forms itself, which may not be the parent's pairs.\",\"The parent analysis is not a matching estimator\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"For a matched design it is the classical answer, and the breakdown Gamma is a single number referees recognise.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"kind\":\"probe\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"observational\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"rosenbaum_bounds\",\"pair_quality\"],\"disrecommend_when\":\"The parent analysis is not a matching estimator\",\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"rbounds\"},\"estimands\":[\"ATT\"],\"explain_key\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"id\":\"probe.rosenbaum\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\"],\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"How unequal could the odds of treatment be inside a matched pair before the conclusion stopped being clear?\",\"options\":[{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The number this probe is about. Filled in automatically when the probe is launched from a result.\",\"label\":\"Parent estimate\",\"name\":\"parent_estimate\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Used to place the parent's confidence interval on the same scale.\",\"label\":\"Parent standard error\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"parent_se\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Which analysis this probe is attached to. Some probes re-run it to get the fitted model rather than just the number.\",\"label\":\"Parent method\",\"name\":\"parent_method\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":3.0,\"help\":\"Gamma is the ratio of treatment odds between two matched units.\",\"label\":\"Largest Gamma to try\",\"max\":20.0,\"min\":1.1,\"name\":\"gamma_max\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.1,\"label\":\"Step\",\"max\":1.0,\"min\":0.01,\"name\":\"gamma_step\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.05,\"label\":\"Level the conclusion is judged at\",\"max\":0.5,\"min\":0.001,\"name\":\"alpha\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"two-sided\",\"greater\",\"less\"],\"default\":\"two-sided\",\"label\":\"Alternative\",\"name\":\"alternative\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"choices\":[\"logit_ps\",\"ps\",\"mahalanobis\"],\"default\":\"logit_ps\",\"help\":\"How the probe forms the 1:1 pairs it bounds.\",\"label\":\"Pair on\",\"name\":\"distance\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"label\":\"Caliper (SD of the score)\",\"max\":2.0,\"min\":0.01,\"name\":\"caliper\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"probes\":[],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:a1f7672f4e91623cf9ed\",\"requested_as\":\"Rosenbaum (2002), Observational Studies, 2nd ed., chapter 4\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1007/978-1-4419-1213-8\",\"requested_as\":\"Rosenbaum (2010), Design of Observational Studies\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"source:unresolved:a1f7672f4e91623cf9ed\",\"10.1007/978-1-4419-1213-8\"],\"references\":[\"Rosenbaum (2002), Observational Studies, 2nd ed., chapter 4\",\"Rosenbaum (2010), Design of Observational Studies\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"cluster\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"outcome\",\"confounders\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/sensitivity.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"2d17c4ca3660d99d91eb0d3bb715c2164c82cc3fe8c8b3d0cf21a2d54c733d8b\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Rosenbaum bounds\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"It bounds bias that operates *within* pairs, and it tests the sharp null of no effect for anybody. The pairs it bounds are the ones it forms itself, which may not be the parent's pairs.\",\"why_recommended\":\"For a matched design it is the classical answer, and the breakdown Gamma is a single number referees recognise.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:079ba4f704df977226c417e0\",\"object_id\":\"concept:design-before-outcome\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:rubin2008\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry e