l context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"rd.kink\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:f965e25071d613e3689fa41f\",\"object_id\":\"diagnostic:bias_correction\",\"predicate\":\"checked_by_diagnostic\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"rd.kink\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:fa417802d36f3bfc8fc6e7ef\",\"object_id\":\"concept:rd-bandwidth\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:cattaneo2022\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"rd.kink\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Where a formula changes slope rather than switching on, measure the change in slope of the outcome.\",\"title\":\"Regression kink (the rule bends, it does not switch)\"}" .
<urn:capy:rd.local_linear> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Sharp RD at the cutoff" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:rd.local_linear\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:rd.local_linear\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1016/j.jeconom.2007.05.001\",\"calonico2014\",\"source:unresolved:179f2828781ef26e5dd8\",\"source:unresolved:afa378e198697172e867\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"rdrobust\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"rdrobust\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.rd\",\"id\":\"rd\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Crossing a score, age, or border switched the programme on.\",\"title\":\"A cutoff decided eligibility\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.rd_plot\",\"id\":\"rd_plot\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Binned scatter at the cutoff\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.bias_correction\",\"id\":\"bias_correction\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Bias correction and robust interval\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.bandwidth_sensitivity\",\"id\":\"bandwidth_sensitivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Bandwidth sensitivity path\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.running_variable_discreteness\",\"id\":\"running_variable_discreteness\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Discreteness of the running variable\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.manipulation\",\"id\":\"manipulation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Density at the cutoff\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.covariate_balance\",\"id\":\"covariate_balance\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Covariate balance\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"LATE\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.late\",\"id\":\"LATE\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who only got it because of the instrument or the cutoff, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Local average treatment effect\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.rd.local_linear\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"rd.local_linear\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Fit a line either side of the threshold and measure the step between them.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":1,\"help\":\"1 is the default and the one the literature defends. Higher orders fit more wiggle inside the window and are easy to over-read.\",\"label\":\"Polynomial order either side\",\"max\":4,\"min\":1,\"name\":\"polynomial_order\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"choices\":[\"mse\",\"ik\"],\"default\":\"mse\",\"help\":\"'mse' is capy's own finite-sample plug-in rule: it measures the bias and variance of this estimator on this sample. 'ik' is the Imbens-Kalyanaraman (2012) formula, for a sharp local linear fit only. Neither is rdrobust's CCT selector.\",\"label\":\"How to choose the window\",\"name\":\"bandwidth_selector\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The half-width of the window either side of the cutoff, in the units of the running variable. Setting it by hand overrides the selector; the sensitivity path shows you what every other choice would have given.\",\"label\":\"Bandwidth (leave empty to choose one)\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"bandwidth\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.0,\"help\":\"Drop units within this distance of the cutoff, where heaping and manipulation live. Every dropped row appears in the sample flow.\",\"label\":\"Donut hole radius\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"donut\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"triangular\",\"epanechnikov\",\"uniform\"],\"default\":\"triangular\",\"help\":\"Triangular gives the most weight to units closest to the cutoff, which is what the MSE-optimal theory assumes. Uniform is the plain 'everyone inside the window counts equally' choice.\",\"label\":\"Weighting near the cutoff\",\"name\":\"kernel\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The wider window used by the higher-order fit that estimates the smoothing bias.\",\"label\":\"Bias-correction pilot bandwidth\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"pilot_bandwidth\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Off by default: in RD the covariates are how you check the design, not how you fix it. Turning this on tightens the interval a little and slightly changes the estimand.\",\"label\":\"Put the covariates in the local regression\",\"name\":\"covariate_adjust\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"HC0\",\"HC1\",\"HC2\",\"HC3\"],\"default\":\"HC1\",\"help\":\"Heteroskedasticity-robust. HC3 is more conservative in small windows. Set the cluster role as well and the variance becomes cluster-robust.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"vce\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"0.95 unless you have a reason.\",\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0,\"help\":\"0 picks about 2 n^(1/3) bins a side.\",\"label\":\"Bins per side in the plot\",\"max\":100,\"min\":0,\"name\":\"plot_bins\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"choices\":[\"quantile\",\"evenly\"],\"default\":\"quantile\",\"help\":\"Quantile bins hold the same number of units each; even bins hold the same width each.\",\"label\":\"Bin spacing\",\"name\":\"plot_bin_spacing\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"}],\"plain_language\":\"Fit a line either side of the threshold and measure the step between them.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.negative_control\",\"id\":\"probe.negative_control\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Estimate something that shares the confounding but not the causal path. A non-zero answer is bias you can see.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.negative_control\",\"title\":\"Negative control\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.subset\",\"id\":\"probe.subset\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Re-estimate on random subsets. The answer should move about as much as losing that much data costs, and no more.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.subset\",\"title\":\"Subset stability\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"}],\"references\":[\"Imbens & Lemieux (2008), Regression discontinuity designs: a guide to practice\",\"Calonico, Cattaneo & Titiunik (2014), Robust nonparametric confidence intervals for regression-discontinuity designs\",\"Imbens & Kalyanaraman (2012), Optimal bandwidth choice for the regression discontinuity estimator\",\"Cattaneo, Idrobo & Titiunik (2020), A practical introduction to regression discontinuity designs\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"an instrument\",\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"at least one measured confounder\",\"a clustering variable\",\"a treatment\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a running variable\",\"a cutoff\",\"an outcome\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.rd\",\"id\":\"rd\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Crossing a score, age, or border switched the programme on.\",\"title\":\"A cutoff decided eligibility\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.rd.fuzzy\",\"id\":\"rd.fuzzy\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Divide the jump in the outcome by the jump in take-up: the effect for the people the cutoff actually moved.\",\"title\":\"Fuzzy RD (crossing the cutoff only nudged people in)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.rd.local_randomization\",\"id\":\"rd.local_randomization\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Treat a narrow window around the cutoff as a small randomised experiment rather than fitting a curve through it.\",\"title\":\"Local randomisation RD\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.rd.multi_cutoff\",\"id\":\"rd.multi_cutoff\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Several thresholds, or a boundary on a map, pooled into one design.\",\"title\":\"Multi-cutoff and geographic RD\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"A cutoff decided eligibility\",\"LATE\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Sharp RD at the cutoff\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.no_manipulation\",\"explains\":\"People could not precisely control which side of the cutoff they landed on.\",\"id\":\"no_manipulation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No manipulation of the running variable\",\"worry_when\":\"A visible spike or gap in the density at the cutoff; covariates that jump; a cutoff that people knew about and had time to respond to.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.continuity\",\"explains\":\"Everything else that affects the outcome changes smoothly through the cutoff, so the only thing that jumps is the treatment.\",\"id\":\"continuity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Continuity of potential outcomes at the cutoff\",\"worry_when\":\"Several rules share the threshold; the running variable is coarse, so \\\"at the cutoff\\\" is really a wide band; the estimate depends heavily on the bandwidth.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.consistency\",\"explains\":\"The outcome you observe under the treatment a unit received is the same as the potential outcome under that treatment. In practice: the treatment has to be a thing someone could actually do.\",\"id\":\"consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined intervention\",\"worry_when\":\"The treatment is a state of the world rather than an action, or it is coded from several very different real interventions.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"The answer is only about units at the cutoff, and it moves with the bandwidth and the polynomial order. If people could see the threshold and push themselves across it, the comparison is gone -- which is why the density test and the covariate jumps travel with the estimate. This is capy.py's own local-polynomial code, not rdrobust. The bandwidth selector is named in the Classic tab and the variance is heteroskedasticity- or cluster-robust rather than rdrobust's nearest-neighbour estimator, so numbers will be close but need not match to the last digit.\",\"The running variable has fewer than about 20 distinct values either side of the cutoff inside the bandwidth\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"When a cutoff really did decide eligibility, the units either side of it are as good as randomly assigned, and you can see the whole argument in one plot. Nothing else in observational work is this legible.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\"],\"id\":\"rd.local_linear\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"rd.local_linear\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"rd\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"rd_plot\",\"bias_correction\",\"bandwidth_sensitivity\",\"running_variable_discreteness\",\"manipulation\",\"covariate_balance\"],\"disrecommend_when\":\"The running variable has fewer than about 20 distinct values either side of the cutoff inside the bandwidth\",\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"rdrobust\"},\"estimands\":[\"LATE\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.rd.local_linear\",\"id\":\"rd.local_linear\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\"],\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Fit a line either side of the threshold and measure the step between them.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":1,\"help\":\"1 is the default and the one the literature defends. Higher orders fit more wiggle inside the window and are easy to over-read.\",\"label\":\"Polynomial order either side\",\"max\":4,\"min\":1,\"name\":\"polynomial_order\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"choices\":[\"mse\",\"ik\"],\"default\":\"mse\",\"help\":\"'mse' is capy's own finite-sample plug-in rule: it measures the bias and variance of this estimator on this sample. 'ik' is the Imbens-Kalyanaraman (2012) formula, for a sharp local linear fit only. Neither is rdrobust's CCT selector.\",\"label\":\"How to choose the window\",\"name\":\"bandwidth_selector\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The half-width of the window either side of the cutoff, in the units of the running variable. Setting it by hand overrides the selector; the sensitivity path shows you what every other choice would have given.\",\"label\":\"Bandwidth (leave empty to choose one)\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"bandwidth\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.0,\"help\":\"Drop units within this distance of the cutoff, where heaping and manipulation live. Every dropped row appears in the sample flow.\",\"label\":\"Donut hole radius\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"donut\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"choices\":[\"triangular\",\"epanechnikov\",\"uniform\"],\"default\":\"triangular\",\"help\":\"Triangular gives the most weight to units closest to the cutoff, which is what the MSE-optimal theory assumes. Uniform is the plain 'everyone inside the window counts equally' choice.\",\"label\":\"Weighting near the cutoff\",\"name\":\"kernel\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"The wider window used by the higher-order fit that estimates the smoothing bias.\",\"label\":\"Bias-correction pilot bandwidth\",\"min\":0.0,\"name\":\"pilot_bandwidth\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Off by default: in RD the covariates are how you check the design, not how you fix it. Turning this on tightens the interval a little and slightly changes the estimand.\",\"label\":\"Put the covariates in the local regression\",\"name\":\"covariate_adjust\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"HC0\",\"HC1\",\"HC2\",\"HC3\"],\"default\":\"HC1\",\"help\":\"Heteroskedasticity-robust. HC3 is more conservative in small windows. Set the cluster role as well and the variance becomes cluster-robust.\",\"label\":\"Standard errors\",\"name\":\"vce\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"0.95 unless you have a reason.\",\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0,\"help\":\"0 picks about 2 n^(1/3) bins a side.\",\"label\":\"Bins per side in the plot\",\"max\":100,\"min\":0,\"name\":\"plot_bins\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"choices\":[\"quantile\",\"evenly\"],\"default\":\"quantile\",\"help\":\"Quantile bins hold the same number of units each; even bins hold the same width each.\",\"label\":\"Bin spacing\",\"name\":\"plot_bin_spacing\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"}],\"probes\":[\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"probe.negative_control\",\"probe.subset\",\"probe.alternate_spec\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1016/j.jeconom.2007.05.001\",\"requested_as\":\"Imbens & Lemieux (2008), Regression discontinuity designs: a guide to practice\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"calonico2014\",\"requested_as\":\"Calonico, Cattaneo & Titiunik (2014), Robust nonparametric confidence intervals for regression-discontinuity designs\"},{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:179f2828781ef26e5dd8\",\"requested_as\":\"Imbens & Kalyanaraman (2012), Optimal bandwidth choice for the regression discontinuity estimator\"},{\"disposition\":\"unresolved_search_only\",\"id\":\"source:unresolved:afa378e198697172e867\",\"requested_as\":\"Cattaneo, Idrobo & Titiunik (2020), A practical introduction to regression discontinuity designs\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"10.1016/j.jeconom.2007.05.001\",\"calonico2014\",\"source:unresolved:179f2828781ef26e5dd8\",\"source:unresolved:afa378e198697172e867\"],\"references\":[\"Imbens & Lemieux (2008), Regression discontinuity designs: a guide to practice\",\"Calonico, Cattaneo & Titiunik (2014), Robust nonparametric confidence intervals for regression-discontinuity designs\",\"Imbens & Kalyanaraman (2012), Optimal bandwidth choice for the regression discontinuity estimator\",\"Cattaneo, Idrobo & Titiunik (2020), A practical introduction to regression discontinuity designs\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"instruments\",\"forbidden\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"confounders\",\"cluster\",\"treatment\"],\"roles_required\":[\"running\",\"cutoff\",\"outcome\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/rd.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"a86f14c44b23637b2b7378f638cdbfba5ad3bdcb0ed99ee9af783e9f071548bf\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Sharp RD at the cutoff\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"The answer is only about units at the cutoff, and it moves with the bandwidth and the polynomial order. If people could see the threshold and push themselves across it, the comparison is gone -- which is why the density test and the covariate jumps travel with the estimate. This is capy.py's own local-polynomial code, not rdrobust. The bandwidth selector is named in the Classic tab and the variance is heteroskedasticity- or cluster-robust rather than rdrobust's nearest-neighbour estimator, so numbers will be close but need not match to the last digit.\",\"why_recommended\":\"When a cutoff really did decide eligibility, the units either side of it are as good as randomly assigned, and you can see the whole argument in one plot. Nothing else in observational work is this legible.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:0169a00918bea6771dd2d31d\",\"object_id\":\"estimand:LATE\",\"predicate\":\"targets_estimand\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"rd.local_linear\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editori