he-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"source_version\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.06.003\",\"summary\":\"Bibliographic metadata/link only; no publication text, abstract, figure or dataset is distributed.\",\"title\":\"Sant’Anna, P. H. C., & Zhao, J. (2020). Doubly robust difference-in-differences estimators. Journal of Econometrics, 219(1), 101–122.\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.06.003\"}" .
<urn:capy:sc.abadie> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Synthetic control" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:sc.abadie\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:sc.abadie\",\"citation_ids\":[\"10.1257/000282803321455188\",\"10.1257/jel.20191450\",\"abadie2010\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"Synth / tidysynth\"},\"needs_r_packages\":[\"Synth / tidysynth\"],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.synth\",\"id\":\"synth\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"One treated unit; build a comparison from a donor pool.\",\"title\":\"One place, constructed twin\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_pre_fit\",\"id\":\"sc_pre_fit\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Pre-treatment fit\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_gap\",\"id\":\"sc_gap\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Treated minus synthetic gap\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_weights\",\"id\":\"sc_weights\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Donor weights\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_convex_hull\",\"id\":\"sc_convex_hull\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Treated unit inside the donor hull\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_placebo_space\",\"id\":\"sc_placebo_space\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Placebo in space\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_placebo_time\",\"id\":\"sc_placebo_time\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Placebo in time\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.sc_loo\",\"id\":\"sc_loo\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Leave one donor out\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"ATT\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.att\",\"id\":\"ATT\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"For people who actually got it, what did it do?\",\"title\":\"Average treatment effect on the treated\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.abadie\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\",\"some of the robustness probes it names have no card of their own yet\"],\"id\":\"sc.abadie\",\"in_more_depth\":null,\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Build a weighted copy of the treated place out of untreated places that looked like it beforehand, then watch the two lines separate.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"cv\",\"prefit\",\"inverse_variance\"],\"default\":\"cv\",\"help\":\"cv: split the pre-treatment period and pick V by held-out fit (the usual choice). prefit: minimise the whole pre-treatment fit (can overfit). inverse_variance: weight predictors equally once standardised.\",\"label\":\"How predictor importance (V) is chosen\",\"name\":\"v_method\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":\"all\",\"help\":\"'all' matches on every pre-treatment period; a number matches on that many evenly spaced lags. Cross-validated V needs a fixed number, so 'all' becomes the length of the training window.\",\"label\":\"Outcome path as predictors\",\"name\":\"outcome_lags\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Variables averaged over the pre-treatment period and matched on alongside the outcome path. Defaults to the confounders on the board.\",\"label\":\"Extra predictors\",\"name\":\"predictors\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Predictors measured over particular periods, e.g. [{'variable': 'gdp', 'periods': [1980, 1985], 'stat': 'mean'}].\",\"label\":\"Special predictors\",\"name\":\"special_predictors\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Re-run the method treating each donor as if it had been treated. This is where the p-value comes from; turning it off leaves the estimate with no yardstick.\",\"label\":\"Placebo in space\",\"name\":\"placebo_in_space\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":60,\"help\":\"Cap on the number of donor placebo refits. Lower it only for speed; the p-value's floor is 1/(placebos+1).\",\"label\":\"Donors used for placebos\",\"max\":500,\"min\":2,\"name\":\"max_placebos\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Refit pretending the intervention happened earlier, using pre-intervention data only.\",\"label\":\"Placebo in time\",\"name\":\"placebo_in_time\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Which earlier period to pretend the intervention happened in. Defaults to about 60% of the way through the pre-treatment period.\",\"label\":\"Placebo date\",\"name\":\"placebo_time\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Refit without each contributing donor, to see whether the result rests on one unit.\",\"label\":\"Leave one donor out\",\"name\":\"leave_one_out\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":30,\"help\":\"Cap on leave-one-donor-out refits.\",\"label\":\"Leave-one-out refits\",\"max\":200,\"min\":1,\"name\":\"max_loo\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":0.5,\"help\":\"Share of total weight at which a single donor raises a warning.\",\"label\":\"Warn when one donor exceeds\",\"max\":1.0,\"min\":0.1,\"name\":\"donor_share_warn\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"Level for the placebo-based interval.\",\"label\":\"Interval level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"plain_language\":\"Build a weighted copy of the treated place out of untreated places that looked like it beforehand, then watch the two lines separate.\",\"probes\":[{\"explain_key\":null,\"id\":\"placebo_in_space\",\"in_catalogue\":false,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":null,\"requested_as\":\"placebo_in_space\",\"title\":\"Placebo in space: run it on a unit that was never treated\"},{\"explain_key\":null,\"id\":\"placebo_in_time\",\"in_catalogue\":false,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":null,\"requested_as\":\"placebo_in_time\",\"title\":\"Placebo in time: pretend it happened earlier\"},{\"explain_key\":null,\"id\":\"leave_one_donor_out\",\"in_catalogue\":false,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":null,\"requested_as\":\"leave_one_donor_out\",\"title\":\"Leave one donor region out\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"id\":\"probe.alternate_spec\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the grid of defensible specifications and sort the answers. The curve is the result, not the one you happened to run.\",\"requested_as\":\"alternate_spec\",\"title\":\"Specification curve\"},{\"explain_key\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"id\":\"probe.placebo_outcome\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"probe\",\"one_liner\":\"Run the same analysis on something the treatment could not have changed. It should find nothing.\",\"requested_as\":\"placebo_outcome\",\"title\":\"Placebo outcome\"}],\"references\":[\"Abadie & Gardeazabal (2003), The Economic Costs of Conflict: A Case Study of the Basque Country\",\"Abadie, Diamond & Hainmueller (2010), Synthetic Control Methods for Comparative Case Studies\",\"Abadie (2021), Using Synthetic Controls: Feasibility, Data Requirements, and Methodological Aspects\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"a running variable\",\"an instrument\",\"a cutoff\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"a treatment\",\"at least one measured confounder\",\"donor_pool\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a unit id\",\"a time variable\",\"an outcome\",\"the treated unit\",\"an intervention time\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.synth\",\"id\":\"synth\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"One treated unit; build a comparison from a donor pool.\",\"title\":\"One place, constructed twin\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.did.synthdid_r\",\"id\":\"did.synthdid_r\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Weight both units and periods, then take a difference-in-differences -- halfway between synthetic control and DiD.\",\"title\":\"Synthetic difference-in-differences (synthdid)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.its.causal_impact\",\"id\":\"its.causal_impact\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Model the counterfactual series with a structural time-series model and control series, and report a posterior rather than an interval.\",\"title\":\"Bayesian structural time series (CausalImpact)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.augmented\",\"id\":\"sc.augmented\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"When no weighted average of the donors can match the treated place, correct the leftover bias with a ridge model and show the size of the correction.\",\"title\":\"Augmented synthetic control\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.matrix_completion\",\"id\":\"sc.matrix_completion\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Treat the missing treated-period outcomes as holes in a panel and fill them in with a low-rank model of what the panel would have done.\",\"title\":\"Matrix completion\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.microsynth\",\"id\":\"sc.microsynth\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Synthetic control when the treated unit is a neighbourhood or a small area and there are many of them.\",\"title\":\"Microsynth (many treated units)\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.scpi\",\"id\":\"sc.scpi\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Confidence intervals for a synthetic control that come from a model of the prediction error rather than from permutation.\",\"title\":\"Prediction intervals for synthetic control (scpi)\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"One place, constructed twin\",\"ATT\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Synthetic control\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.donor_fit\",\"explains\":\"The weighted combination of untreated units reproduces the treated unit's pre-period path closely enough to stand in for it afterwards.\",\"id\":\"donor_fit\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Pre-treatment fit from the donor pool\",\"worry_when\":\"Visible pre-period gaps; a short pre-period relative to the number of donors; one donor carrying most of the weight.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.convex_hull\",\"explains\":\"The treated unit's characteristics can be written as a weighted average of the donors', with weights that do not go negative.\",\"id\":\"convex_hull\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Treated unit inside the donor convex hull\",\"worry_when\":\"The treated unit is at an extreme of the donor distribution on the predictors, or the pre-period gap has a persistent level offset.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.no_anticipation\",\"explains\":\"Units did not change behaviour before treatment arrived because they knew it was coming.\",\"id\":\"no_anticipation\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No anticipation\",\"worry_when\":\"There was a public announcement well before the policy started, or the pre-period coefficients move in the period immediately before adoption.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.sutva\",\"explains\":\"One unit's treatment does not change another unit's outcome, and \\\"treated\\\" means the same thing for everyone who got it.\",\"id\":\"sutva\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"SUTVA / no interference\",\"worry_when\":\"Units interact: they compete for the same jobs, infect each other, share a classroom or a market. Or the \\\"programme\\\" is really a family of programmes whose intensity varied a lot across sites.\"}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"If the donors cannot reproduce the treated unit before the intervention, the gap afterwards is fit error wearing a policy costume. Weights that pile onto one donor make this a two-unit comparison. With few donors the permutation test cannot produce a small p-value however large the effect, and a donor that had its own shock around the intervention contaminates the comparison. This implementation solves the weight problem with projected gradient plus SLSQP rather than Synth's own solvers, and its cross-validated V is a bounded search, not a global optimum.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"For one treated unit and a run of pre-treatment periods this is the standard, and its output is legible to non-specialists: a line, a shadow line, and the distance between them. The weights are transparent, so a reader can argue with the comparison rather than with a coefficient.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[\"no plain-language description has been written yet, so the one-line summary is standing in for it\",\"some of the robustness probes it names have no card of their own yet\"],\"id\":\"sc.abadie\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"sc.abadie\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"synth\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"sc_pre_fit\",\"sc_gap\",\"sc_weights\",\"sc_convex_hull\",\"sc_placebo_space\",\"sc_placebo_time\",\"sc_loo\"],\"disrecommend_when\":null,\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":\"Synth / tidysynth\"},\"estimands\":[\"ATT\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.sc.abadie\",\"id\":\"sc.abadie\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"pandas\"],\"needs_overlap\":true,\"one_liner\":\"Build a weighted copy of the treated place out of untreated places that looked like it beforehand, then watch the two lines separate.\",\"options\":[{\"choices\":[\"cv\",\"prefit\",\"inverse_variance\"],\"default\":\"cv\",\"help\":\"cv: split the pre-treatment period and pick V by held-out fit (the usual choice). prefit: minimise the whole pre-treatment fit (can overfit). inverse_variance: weight predictors equally once standardised.\",\"label\":\"How predictor importance (V) is chosen\",\"name\":\"v_method\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":\"all\",\"help\":\"'all' matches on every pre-treatment period; a number matches on that many evenly spaced lags. Cross-validated V needs a fixed number, so 'all' becomes the length of the training window.\",\"label\":\"Outcome path as predictors\",\"name\":\"outcome_lags\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Variables averaged over the pre-treatment period and matched on alongside the outcome path. Defaults to the confounders on the board.\",\"label\":\"Extra predictors\",\"name\":\"predictors\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Predictors measured over particular periods, e.g. [{'variable': 'gdp', 'periods': [1980, 1985], 'stat': 'mean'}].\",\"label\":\"Special predictors\",\"name\":\"special_predictors\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Re-run the method treating each donor as if it had been treated. This is where the p-value comes from; turning it off leaves the estimate with no yardstick.\",\"label\":\"Placebo in space\",\"name\":\"placebo_in_space\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":60,\"help\":\"Cap on the number of donor placebo refits. Lower it only for speed; the p-value's floor is 1/(placebos+1).\",\"label\":\"Donors used for placebos\",\"max\":500,\"min\":2,\"name\":\"max_placebos\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Refit pretending the intervention happened earlier, using pre-intervention data only.\",\"label\":\"Placebo in time\",\"name\":\"placebo_in_time\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Which earlier period to pretend the intervention happened in. Defaults to about 60% of the way through the pre-treatment period.\",\"label\":\"Placebo date\",\"name\":\"placebo_time\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"default\":true,\"help\":\"Refit without each contributing donor, to see whether the result rests on one unit.\",\"label\":\"Leave one donor out\",\"name\":\"leave_one_out\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"default\":30,\"help\":\"Cap on leave-one-donor-out refits.\",\"label\":\"Leave-one-out refits\",\"max\":200,\"min\":1,\"name\":\"max_loo\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":0.5,\"help\":\"Share of total weight at which a single donor raises a warning.\",\"label\":\"Warn when one donor exceeds\",\"max\":1.0,\"min\":0.1,\"name\":\"donor_share_warn\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"help\":\"Level for the placebo-based interval.\",\"label\":\"Interval level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"advanced\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"probes\":[\"placebo_in_space\",\"placebo_in_time\",\"leave_one_donor_out\",\"alternate_spec\",\"placebo_outcome\"],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1257/000282803321455188\",\"requested_as\":\"Abadie & Gardeazabal (2003), The Economic Costs of Conflict: A Case Study of the Basque Country\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"abadie2010\",\"requested_as\":\"Abadie, Diamond & Hainmueller (2010), Synthetic Control Methods for Comparative Case Studies\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"10.1257/jel.20191450\",\"requested_as\":\"Abadie (2021), Using Synthetic Controls: Feasibility, Data Requirements, and Methodological Aspects\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"10.1257/000282803321455188\",\"abadie2010\",\"10.1257/jel.20191450\"],\"references\":[\"Abadie & Gardeazabal (2003), The Economic Costs of Conflict: A Case Study of the Basque Country\",\"Abadie, Diamond & Hainmueller (2010), Synthetic Control Methods for Comparative Case Studies\",\"Abadie (2021), Using Synthetic Controls: Feasibility, Data Requirements, and Methodological Aspects\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"running\",\"instruments\",\"cutoff\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"treatment\",\"confounders\",\"donor_pool\"],\"roles_required\":[\"unit\",\"time\",\"outcome\",\"treated_unit\",\"event_time\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/synth.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"15e0fecaebae31df3c3744e9641e14d8600985ef540e9ec544eefab910067860\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Synthetic control\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"If the donors cannot reproduce the treated unit before the intervention, the gap afterwards is fit error wearing a policy costume. Weights that pile onto one donor make this a two-unit comparison. With few donors the permutation test cannot produce a small p-value however large the effect, and a donor that had its own shock around the intervention contaminates the comparison. This implementation solves the weight problem with projected gradient plus SLSQP rather than Synth's own solvers, and its cross-validated V is a bounded search, not a global optimum.\",\"why_recommended\":\"For one treated unit and a run of pre-treatment periods this is the standard, and its output is legible to non-specialists: a line, a shadow line, and the distance between them. The weights are transparent, so a reader can argue with the comparison rather than with a coefficient.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:14615cd1c17ab2c612a528a3\",\"object_id\":\"concept:anticipation\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"abadie2005\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"sc.abadie\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:1a825b769a2e54e4880d9fd8\",\"object_id\":\"diagnostic:sc_pre_fit\",\"predicate\":\"checked_by_diagnostic\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"sc.abadie\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:1bfe7a4f1193de820e4e4f64\",\"object_id\":\"diagnostic:sc_gap\",\"predicate\":\"checked_by_diagnostic\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"d