 Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"survival.aft\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[\"Interpret the relation within the stated design, population and observation process.\"],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[\"This editorial link does not certify semantic entailment or implementation correctness.\"],\"id\":\"relation:fe26e55a024325bf09ac25f8\",\"object_id\":\"concept:interval-censoring\",\"predicate\":\"related_to\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-ontology\",\"source:ontology:r-survreg\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"basis\":[\"Original explanation and primary reference context; not a completed implementation audit.\"],\"date\":\"2026-10-13\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"agent_editorial_context\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Editorial methodological context for this registry entry; not a reviewed implementation or equivalence assertion.\",\"subject_id\":\"survival.aft\"},{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:feb371d9aabcaec8051055e2\",\"object_id\":\"design:survival\",\"predicate\":\"compatible_with_design\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"scope\":\"Declared project registry/navigation relationship; not an identified causal effect.\",\"subject_id\":\"survival.aft\"}],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export\":true},\"review_basis\":\"Original or imported Apache-2.0 project material; no third-party paper body included.\"},\"summary\":\"Fit a right-censored common-scale log-normal or Weibull AFT model, then distinguish its conditional time factor from marginal standardized survival and RMST.\",\"title\":\"Censored AFT regression and causal standardization\"}" .
<urn:capy:survival.kaplan_meier> a capy:method ; skos:prefLabel "Unadjusted Kaplan–Meier survival contrast" ; prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:capy:source%3Aproject-inventory> ; capy:record "{\"aliases\":[\"method:survival.kaplan_meier\"],\"catalogue_key\":\"method:survival.kaplan_meier\",\"citation_ids\":[\"kaplan1958\",\"uno2014\"],\"citations\":[],\"content\":{\"availability\":{\"coming\":null,\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":false},\"needs_r_packages\":[],\"runs_here\":true,\"summary\":\"Runs on this computer with what the app already installs.\"},\"designs\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.survival\",\"id\":\"survival\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Follow people from a common time zero; some leave follow-up before the event is observed.\",\"title\":\"Time until an event\"}],\"diagnostics\":[{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.survival_followup\",\"id\":\"survival_followup\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Follow-up and common horizon support\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.survival_censoring\",\"id\":\"survival_censoring\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Right-censoring assumptions\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.survival_curves\",\"id\":\"survival_curves\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Observed Kaplan–Meier curves\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.survival_heterogeneity\",\"id\":\"survival_heterogeneity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Baseline subgroup heterogeneity in survival contrasts\"}],\"estimands\":[{\"acronym\":\"S(1) - S(0)\",\"explain_key\":\"estimand.survival_difference\",\"id\":\"survival_difference\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"estimand\",\"one_liner\":\"At a chosen horizon, how do event-free probabilities differ between baseline treatments?\",\"title\":\"Survival probability difference\"}],\"explain_key\":\"method.survival.kaplan_meier\",\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"survival.kaplan_meier\",\"in_more_depth\":\"Events are processed before censoring at tied times. Independent censoring within each group is required for the raw curves. Independence only conditional on other prognostic covariates does not suffice. The app requires a common supported horizon and explicit time unit, reports censoring/risk-set counts and uses seeded within-group subject bootstrap intervals. Bootstrap samples without horizon support are refused and reported. An optional prespecified categorical baseline modifier forms subgroup contrasts, with resampling within each treatment-by-subgroup cell and a direct equality test at the same horizon. Baseline covariates are not adjusted by this method.\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Compare observed group event-free probabilities at an explicit common horizon; this is an unadjusted association.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Optional: one prespecified categorical baseline column with 2–8 observed levels. Tests differences between treatment contrasts on the selected scale at the chosen horizon. No automatic cutpoint search.\",\"label\":\"Baseline subgroup modifier\",\"max_items\":1,\"name\":\"subgroups\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Confirm only when the modifier was measured before treatment and its analysis was specified before inspecting outcomes. Your declaration is recorded but cannot verify the study design.\",\"label\":\"Modifier is baseline and analysis was prespecified\",\"name\":\"subgroups_prespecified\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"days\",\"weeks\",\"months\",\"years\"],\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Choose explicitly. Follow-up duration and the common horizon must use the same time unit.\",\"label\":\"Duration time unit\",\"name\":\"time_unit\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Choose a positive time in the duration column's units, supported in both groups. Set before viewing the contrast. Required for survival/RMST; unused for the conditional time ratio.\",\"label\":\"Common follow-up horizon\",\"min\":0,\"name\":\"horizon\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":100,\"help\":\"Seeded independent-subject resampling; increase for a less noisy interval.\",\"label\":\"Bootstrap resamples\",\"max\":2000,\"min\":20,\"name\":\"bootstrap_reps\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"plain_language\":\"The product-limit estimator accounts for right censoring in observed groups; their probability difference at tau is an association.\",\"probes\":[],\"references\":[\"Kaplan and Meier (1958), Nonparametric Estimation from Incomplete Observations\",\"Uno et al. (2014), Moving Beyond the Hazard Ratio in Quantifying the Between-Group Difference in Survival Analysis\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"entry\",\"start\",\"stop\",\"competing_event\",\"censoring\",\"a clustering variable\",\"weight\",\"strata\",\"a time variable\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"a unit id\"],\"roles_required\":[\"a treatment\",\"elapsed follow-up duration\",\"an event indicator (1 event, 0 right censored)\"],\"see_also\":[{\"explain_key\":\"design.survival\",\"id\":\"survival\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"design\",\"one_liner\":\"Follow people from a common time zero; some leave follow-up before the event is observed.\",\"title\":\"Time until an event\"},{\"explain_key\":\"method.survival.aft\",\"id\":\"survival.aft\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"method\",\"one_liner\":\"Fit a right-censored log-normal/Weibull AFT model; standardize survival/RMST over baseline covariates under explicit causal assumptions, or report a conditional time factor.\",\"title\":\"Censored AFT regression and causal standardization\"},{\"explain_key\":\"concept.survival_censoring\",\"id\":\"concept.survival_censoring\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"concept\",\"one_liner\":\"Right censoring means follow-up ends before the event is observed; the event time remains unknown.\",\"title\":\"Censoring is an observation mechanism\"},{\"explain_key\":\"diagnostic.survival_heterogeneity\",\"id\":\"survival_heterogeneity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"diagnostic\",\"title\":\"Baseline subgroup heterogeneity in survival contrasts\"}],\"status\":\"recommended\",\"status_label\":\"Recommended\",\"tags\":[\"Time until an event\",\"S(1) - S(0)\",\"Recommended\"],\"title\":\"Unadjusted Kaplan–Meier survival contrast\",\"what_it_assumes\":[{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.exchangeability\",\"explains\":\"Treated and untreated units are comparable once you condition on the confounders you measured. Everything that pushed people towards treatment and also moves the outcome is in your adjustment set.\",\"id\":\"exchangeability\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Exchangeability / no unmeasured confounding\",\"worry_when\":\"Treatment was chosen by people who knew something about the likely outcome that you do not observe. Clinical judgement, self-selection into a programme, and administrative triage are the classic cases.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.positivity\",\"explains\":\"Every kind of unit had some chance of being treated and some chance of not being treated. Where that fails, there is no comparison to make and the model is inventing one.\",\"id\":\"positivity\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Positivity / overlap\",\"worry_when\":\"Any single weight carries a large share of the total; the effective sample is far below the nominal one; the propensity model separates the arms almost perfectly; treated units sit outside the control group's range.\"},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.survival_consistency\",\"explains\":\"Observed event times must agree with the potential event times under the treatment actually received, with meaningful treatment versions.\",\"id\":\"survival_consistency\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Consistency / well-defined baseline intervention\",\"worry_when\":null},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.survival_no_interference\",\"explains\":\"One person's event time is assumed unaffected by other people's treatment assignments.\",\"id\":\"survival_no_interference\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"No interference between people\",\"worry_when\":null},{\"explain_key\":\"assumption.conditional_independent_censoring\",\"explains\":\"Given baseline treatment and covariates, censoring must not convey additional information about the unobserved event time.\",\"id\":\"conditional_independent_censoring\",\"in_catalogue\":true,\"kind\":\"assumption\",\"title\":\"Independent censoring conditional on treatment and baseline covariates\",\"worry_when\":null}],\"when_not_to_use\":[\"Single event, right censoring, baseline treatment and independent subjects only. Time zero and event definition must agree across groups. A sparse tail, informative censoring, competing events or confounding invalidates a naive causal reading.\"],\"when_to_use\":[\"Makes censoring and the chosen time horizon visible before interpreting a contrast.\"]},\"disposition\":\"imported\",\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"survival.kaplan_meier\",\"kind\":\"method\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"raw_id\":\"survival.kaplan_meier\",\"registry\":{\"designs\":[\"survival\"],\"diagnostics\":[\"survival_followup\",\"survival_censoring\",\"survival_curves\",\"survival_heterogeneity\"],\"engine_support_basis\":\"Static adapter decorator and declared package metadata; installed availability not checked.\",\"engines\":{\"python\":true,\"r\":false},\"estimands\":[\"survival_difference\"],\"explain_key\":\"method.survival.kaplan_meier\",\"id\":\"survival.kaplan_meier\",\"needs\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\"],\"needs_overlap\":false,\"one_liner\":\"Compare observed group event-free probabilities at an explicit common horizon; this is an unadjusted association.\",\"options\":[{\"default\":[],\"help\":\"Optional: one prespecified categorical baseline column with 2–8 observed levels. Tests differences between treatment contrasts on the selected scale at the chosen horizon. No automatic cutpoint search.\",\"label\":\"Baseline subgroup modifier\",\"max_items\":1,\"name\":\"subgroups\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"columns\"},{\"default\":false,\"help\":\"Confirm only when the modifier was measured before treatment and its analysis was specified before inspecting outcomes. Your declaration is recorded but cannot verify the study design.\",\"label\":\"Modifier is baseline and analysis was prespecified\",\"name\":\"subgroups_prespecified\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"bool\"},{\"choices\":[\"days\",\"weeks\",\"months\",\"years\"],\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Choose explicitly. Follow-up duration and the common horizon must use the same time unit.\",\"label\":\"Duration time unit\",\"name\":\"time_unit\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"select\"},{\"default\":null,\"help\":\"Choose a positive time in the duration column's units, supported in both groups. Set before viewing the contrast. Required for survival/RMST; unused for the conditional time ratio.\",\"label\":\"Common follow-up horizon\",\"min\":0,\"name\":\"horizon\",\"profile\":\"beginner\",\"type\":\"number\"},{\"default\":100,\"help\":\"Seeded independent-subject resampling; increase for a less noisy interval.\",\"label\":\"Bootstrap resamples\",\"max\":2000,\"min\":20,\"name\":\"bootstrap_reps\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"default\":0.95,\"label\":\"Confidence level\",\"max\":0.999,\"min\":0.5,\"name\":\"ci_level\",\"profile\":\"standard\",\"type\":\"number\"}],\"probes\":[],\"reference_dispositions\":[{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"kaplan1958\",\"requested_as\":\"Kaplan and Meier (1958), Nonparametric Estimation from Incomplete Observations\"},{\"disposition\":\"resolved_metadata\",\"id\":\"uno2014\",\"requested_as\":\"Uno et al. (2014), Moving Beyond the Hazard Ratio in Quantifying the Between-Group Difference in Survival Analysis\"}],\"reference_ids\":[\"kaplan1958\",\"uno2014\"],\"references\":[\"Kaplan and Meier (1958), Nonparametric Estimation from Incomplete Observations\",\"Uno et al. (2014), Moving Beyond the Hazard Ratio in Quantifying the Between-Group Difference in Survival Analysis\"],\"roles_forbidden\":[\"entry\",\"start\",\"stop\",\"competing_event\",\"censoring\",\"cluster\",\"weight\",\"strata\",\"time\"],\"roles_optional\":[\"unit\"],\"roles_required\":[\"treatment\",\"duration\",\"event\"],\"source_path\":\"engines/python/capy_py/survival.py\",\"source_sha256\":\"87715ef1c40348535ad9e46db59851f0b6530b69f5970a4f2c7a0041f68f80ba\",\"status\":\"recommended\",\"title\":\"Unadjusted Kaplan–Meier survival contrast\",\"what_can_go_wrong\":\"Single event, right censoring, baseline treatment and independent subjects only. Time zero and event definition must agree across groups. A sparse tail, informative censoring, competing events or confounding invalidates a naive causal reading.\",\"why_recommended\":\"Makes censoring and the chosen time horizon visible before interpreting a contrast.\"},\"relations\":[{\"assertion_mode\":\"editorial\",\"conditions\":[],\"counterevidence\":[],\"gaps\":[],\"id\":\"relation:042671d4a9302526fbbe10cb\",\"object_id\":\"softwarepackage:capy-python\",\"predicate\":\"implemented_by\",\"provenance\":[\"source:project-inventory\"],\"review\":{\"actor\":\"Codex agent\",\"actor_type\":\"agent\",\"date\":\"2026-10-12\",\"human_review\":false,\"semantic\":\"not_assessed\",\"structural\":\"validated\"},\"rights\":{\"attribution\":\"Causal Capybara contributors; Yusufhan Balci; VCESR\",\"content_type\":\"original_project_content\",\"license_id\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"license_url\":\"https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\",\"modified\":true,\"permissions\":{\"adapt\":true,\"cache\":true,\"display\":true,\"model_context\":true,\"public_export